      "message": "Thanks for looking into it and sort out something can work!\nas we talked offline, let\u0027s try avoid accessing bta/ag directly.\n\nA proper way to solve this could be copy what\u0027s done in \"bta/hfp_client\" (the other side of HFP role, i.e the headset) which exposes BTHF_CLIENT_AUDIO_STATE_CONNECTED_MSBC.\n\nDid a quick code trace:\n// how it works now\nIn `bta/ag/bta_ag_sco.cc` function bta_ag_sco_conn_open() emits BTA_AG_AUDIO_OPEN_EVT event.\nIn `src/btif_hf.cc` triggers\nbt_hf_callbacks-\u003eAudioStateCallback(BTHF_AUDIO_STATE_CONNECTED, ...)\n\n// how to extend this\nIn bta_ag_sco can check `p_scb-\u003esco_codec \u003d\u003d MSBC` and emit a new BTA_AG_AUDIO_OPEN_MSBC_EVT\nThen in btif_hf.cc accordingly, hook a new BTHF_AUDIO_STATE_CONNECTED_MSBC event.\n\nFinally in the bluetooth_media/hfp_shim layer we can have additional value to `self.hfp_audio_state` and get_hfp_audio_started() can pass MSBC or not back to CRAS.",
